Interesting — the second test's comment says "a kimi and an openai entry one host stay separate records... and two chatgpt records on different endpoints never merge" but the test body creates two OPENAI entries with DIFFERENT names ('lab', 'lab-2') on the same host. Actually with name-based identity, 'lab' vs 'lab-2' are different names → different identities regardless. This test doesn't even exercise the interesting cases it describes in the comment (kimi same name; two chatgpt entries with different endpoints). A same-name kimi pair WOULD merge by canonical name (pre-existing #706 behavior). The comment mismatches the test body — worth a SUGESTION.

